From: Thingino <dev@thingino.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hal: poll the encoder non-blocking on T31 (open-tx-isp)

On the T31 with the open-tx-isp driver, libimp's blocking
IMP_Encoder_PollingStream path (timeout > 0) clobbers a callee-saved
register in the caller: measured with a minimal harness, s0 comes back
wild after a blocking poll and the next instruction faults
(si_addr=0). video_thread then crashes right after "video chn%d
streaming" and the encoder never streams.

Poll non-blocking (timeout 0) and yield instead. Verified on
cinnado_d1_t31l_sc2336_atbm6031 (5.15 open-tx-isp): stable RTSP stream,
encoder IRQ advancing, no SIGSEGV.

--- a/src/hal/hal_ingenic.c
+++ b/src/hal/hal_ingenic.c
@@ -2597,7 +2597,16 @@
         }
         /* honor IDR requests from RTSP/HTTP threads here (single-thread IMP) */
         if (vc->idr_req){ vc->idr_req=0; IMP_Encoder_RequestIDR(vc->chn); }
+#if defined(PLATFORM_T31)
+        /* T31 open-tx-isp: libimp's PollingStream blocking path (timeout>0)
+         * clobbers a callee-saved register in the caller (measured: the
+         * caller's s0 comes back wild after a blocking poll, and video_thread
+         * then faults). Poll non-blocking and yield instead. */
+        int pr = IMP_Encoder_PollingStream(vc->chn, 0);
+        if (pr != 0) usleep(2000);
+#else
         int pr = IMP_Encoder_PollingStream(vc->chn, g_hcfg->imp_polling_timeout);
+#endif
         IMPEncoderStream st;
 #if defined(PLATFORM_T40)||defined(PLATFORM_T41)
         /* ABI tripwire (same idea as the T23 fcrop store in fs_create): the
